2026-10-19  boot.py is gone: prebsd.c drives every image (Unix and TOPS-10), retries a
            boot that hangs, can keep an image running (-k, -S), and uses simh/bin/ and the
            local mirror.  build-simh builds the simulators from pinned sources; mirror-built
            keeps the disks made from tapes.

prebsd ChangeLog
===============

The authoritative history is the git log.  Summary:

  2026-08-27  Added V4/V5 and 32V to the manifest; converted it to JSON with
              provenance, mount commands and sha256 checksums; fetch skips or
              re-downloads by checksum and keeps mismatched files for
              investigation.
  2026-08-26  Split the simh console driver out of filsys into its own repo;
              added fetch + images.json manifest + ini/ per-image configs +
              boot.py.
